 'baseline' is undefined.","No AC or test covers create_defaults emission, so the boundary is unverified as well."],"finding":"'create_defaults stubs for required-beyond-baseline create fields' does not define what the 'baseline' set of create fields is, leaving the executor to decide which fields count as beyond-baseline.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f3dfd34ff0281658f","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach / 'create_defaults stubs for required-beyond-baseline create fields'","norm_id":"na5b41ab69585bc60","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Executor must decide whether summary/project/issuetype (always-required) count as baseline vs. custom required fields."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"State: 'baseline = the always-required createmeta fields (project, issuetype, summary); create_defaults stubs are emitted only for required fields OUTSIDE that baseline.'","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.75,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Reconcile the proposed `rebar bridge probe <PROJECT>` with the existing `bridge probe`/`bridge-probe` (canonical `rebar bridge check-access`) capability preflight — choose a non-colliding verb or explicitly state how the read-only mapping probe coexists with the existing issue-creating one.","cohort":["E4"],"criteria":["E4"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.1,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan quote: 'Add a read-only probe under the bridge command surface: rebar bridge probe <PROJECT>' and 'it stays strictly read-only against Jira.'","src/rebar/_cli/help/bridge-probe.txt:3-4: 'Live Jira capability preflight ... Creates and deletes a throwaway issue.'","src/rebar/_cli/__init__.py:103-109: `_bridge_probe` is `rebar bridge check-access` → live Jira capability preflight that 'creates + deletes a throwaway issue'.","src/rebar/_cli/_registry.py:579 registers 'bridge-probe'; CHANGELOG.md:74-76 confirms 'bridge-probe' is a live-capability alias, distinct from the mapping-audit `bridge fsck`/`bridge setup`."],"finding":"The plan proposes 'A new probe ... rebar bridge probe <PROJECT>' that 'stays strictly read-only', but a `bridge probe`/`bridge-probe` command already exists — canonical `rebar bridge check-access` — and it is NOT read-only: its docstring and help say it 'Creates and deletes a throwaway issue' as a live capability preflight. The plan neither acknowledges the existing command nor resolves the name collision and the read-only-vs-mutating contradiction.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f9560fbf8d5e87545","impact":0.85,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach / Scope — 'rebar bridge probe <PROJECT>' and 'rebar bridge probe CLI wiring in the bridge command surface'","norm_id":"n1b30505a92d83cb0","priority":0.85,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["`rebar bridge probe` is invoked and dispatches to the existing mutating capability preflight (or the new subcommand shadows/collides with the alias), surprising operators who expected a read-only mapping emit."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Rename the new command (e.g. `rebar bridge suggest-mapping <PROJECT>` or `bridge probe-mapping`) to avoid colliding with the existing mutating `bridge probe`/`bridge-probe` capability preflight.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Resolve the `probe` verb-name collision: `probe`/`bridge-probe` is a retired alias for `bridge check-access` and held-out tests (test_bridge_cli_heldout.py:130, test_bridge_vocabulary_heldout.py:28, test_bridge_vocabulary_stale_heldout.py:107) assert it is not a live bridge verb — either pick a non-colliding verb (e.g. `bridge map-suggest`) or enumerate and update every affected test/doc consumer in Scope.","cohort":["G1G2"],"criteria":["G1G2"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.15,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["tests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_cli_heldout.py:130 — `for future_verb in (\"resolve\", \"probe\", \"bind\", \"unbind\"): assert not re.search(... future_verb ...)` — asserts 'probe' does not appear on the bridge verb surface","tests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_vocabulary_heldout.py:28 — `(['bridge','check-access'], ['bridge-probe'], 'rebar._cli._bridge_probe')` — bridge-probe is a LEGACY alias for check-access","tests/interfaces/contracts/test_bridge_vocabulary_stale_heldout.py:107 — `('bridge-probe', 'bridge check-access')` migration pairing","docs/release-notes.md:201 & docs/exit-codes.md:164 — 'bridge-probe -> bridge check-access' compatibility alias","Bridge parser at src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/advanced/bridge.py registers preview/run/sync/status/pause/resume/fsck/check-access/setup/projects — 'probe' is deliberately absent","Plan Scope enumerates only the new module, CLI wiring, and test_probe.py — no citation of a prerequisite ticket licensing the name, and no listing of these held-out consumers"],"finding":"The plan introduces `rebar bridge probe <PROJECT>` as a NEW live bridge verb, but `probe`/`bridge-probe` is an established RETIRED compatibility alias for `bridge check-access`; existing held-out/vocabulary tests outside the plan's named dirs assert `probe` is NOT a live bridge verb and are not enumerated as consumers the change must update.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f1bcc9a090f8161c1","impact":0.85,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach / Scope — 'rebar bridge probe <PROJECT>' and 'rebar bridge probe CLI wiring in the bridge command surface'","norm_id":"n74cbf46efcb1963f","priority":0.85,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Wiring `bridge probe` into the bridge parser flips these held-out assertions from pass to fail","A reader/maintainer conflates the new live verb with the retired `bridge-probe` -> `check-access` alias, producing ambiguous CLI vocabulary and doc contradictions"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Rename the command to a verb not already retired (e.g. `rebar bridge map-suggest <PROJECT>` or `rebar bridge discover-mapping <PROJECT>`), OR add the affected held-out/vocabulary tests and docs (test_bridge_cli_heldout.py, test_bridge_vocabulary_heldout.py, test_bridge_vocabulary_stale_heldout.py, docs/release-notes.md, docs/exit-codes.md, docs/cli-reference.md, src/rebar/_cli/help/bridge.txt) to Scope as consumers this change must update.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Name the serialization mechanism `--write` uses to emit the nested `[mapping.projects.<KEY>.*]` block while preserving existing comments/hand edits (the existing `_emit_toml` raises `ConfigError` on nested sub-tables and drops comments), and specify the deep-merge/atomic-replace strategy.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.4,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: '--write merges it into the resolved config file under projects.<KEY> (never clobbering existing hand edits -- deep-merge, existing keys win)'","src/rebar/_config_writer.py:32-89 _emit_toml is 'deliberately NOT a general TOML writer (no inline tables, no nested tables...)' and raises ConfigError: 'cannot serialize nested sub-table [{name}.{key}]; rebar's config writer supports only top-level keys and one level of [section]'","src/rebar/_config_writer.py:49-51: 'comments are not preserved' -- conflicts with the plan's 'never clobbering existing hand edits' promise if it reuses this writer","The mapping block is [mapping.projects.<KEY>.status_map] etc. (4+ nesting levels), beyond the one-level-section writer","resolve_symbol confirms tomlkit IS installed (supports nested tables + comment preservation), so a correct mechanism exists but is unnamed"],"finding":"The --write path promises a deep-merge into the nested [mapping.projects.<KEY>.*] block that preserves existing hand edits/comments, but names no serialization mechanism capable of emitting that nesting; the repo's only config writer cannot do it.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f9280898608332d3f","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach section ('--write merges it into the resolved config file under projects.<KEY> ... deep-merge, existing keys win') and Scope ('a neutral emit/merge helper')","norm_id":"n4ec33c8592b5fe60","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["`rebar bridge probe REB --write` against an existing rebar.toml that already carries a hand-edited [mapping.projects.REB.status_map]","A first-time --write that must create the nested projects.<KEY> subtables from scratch"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"State that `--write` uses `tomlkit` (already installed) for a comment-preserving read-modify-write: parse the resolved config file, deep-merge the discovered maps under `projects.<KEY>` with existing keys winning, and atomically replace the file -- rather than the top-level-only `_config_writer._emit_toml`. Add a test asserting an inline comment on an existing `status_map` entry survives `--write`.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"high","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"State which Jira deployment(s) the probe targets (Cloud v3 vs. Data Center v2) and how it selects the API-version path prefix and handles deployment-specific field availability (e.g. hierarchyLevel absent on DC).","cohort":["T3"],"criteria":["T3"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.23,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'proved every axis is interrogable read-only via Jira REST v3'","Plan names '/issuetype (hierarchyLevel)' — hierarchyLevel is a Jira Cloud-shaped field","scripts/jira_dc_capability_map.py uses /rest/api/2/issuetype, /rest/api/2/priority, /rest/api/2/issueLinkType throughout for Data Center","src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira/acli.py uses /rest/api/3/... for Cloud","_direct_rest_get(path) takes a full path including the version segment, so the version is a caller responsibility the plan leaves unspecified"],"finding":"The plan asserts 'Jira REST v3' and relies on endpoint paths/fields (e.g. hierarchyLevel on /issuetype, /project/{key}/statuses) that differ between Jira Cloud (/rest/api/3) and Jira Data Center (/rest/api/2), but never states which deployment the probe targets — the codebase drives both (the DC capability-map script uses /rest/api/2 while the Cloud adapter uses /rest/api/3).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f697fc7f4eeeeeb74","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach / Context section ('interrogable read-only via Jira REST v3')","norm_id":"n0aa22e30df2050d6","priority":0.67,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An operator runs `rebar bridge probe` against a Jira Data Center instance where the v3 paths 404 or /issuetype omits hierarchyLevel, silently producing an incomplete or empty mapping block"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify that --write follows ADR 0070's target rule (rebar-owned rebar.toml, never a user pyproject.toml), and how the write reconciles with the existing write path's target selection.","cohort":["A1"],"criteria":["A1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.3637,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["docs/adr/0070-jira-onboard-config-write.md Decision 1: 'Never edit a user-owned pyproject.toml. The write target is always a rebar-owned rebar.toml'","The 'resolved config file' can be a pyproject.toml [tool.rebar] table per _discover_project_config"],"finding":"The --write target is described as 'the resolved config file', but ADR 0070 requires the write path to NEVER edit a user-owned pyproject.toml and always persist to a rebar-owned rebar.toml.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ff56747bedd80337a","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach ('--write merges it into the resolved config file under projects.<KEY>')","norm_id":"ndadeeeae50855885","priority":0.5863,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Operator runs --write in a repo whose config lives in pyproject.toml; the probe rewrites the user's pyproject, violating the ADR"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"high","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify how the probe surfaces a failed/unreachable Jira endpoint or unknown project key (fail with a clear diagnostic; do not emit a partial mapping silently).","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e"],"criteria":["T5b"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.4894,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["The plan lists five endpoints called in sequence with no mention of what happens when one returns an error, is unreachable, or the PROJECT does not exist.","Testing section only fakes canned success responses and the recorded method set — no failure-path oracle."],"finding":"The probe issues several live Jira GET requests but the plan does not describe error handling / surfacing when an endpoint fails, times out, or the project key is unknown (e.g. 404 on /project/{key}/statuses).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f6416edf5fa2196e1","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach / 'It calls the proven endpoints'","norm_id":"n84cd2b197fbedda0","priority":0.4606,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["User runs `rebar bridge probe BADKEY`; a 404/timeout occurs on one of the five endpoints mid-probe."],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.6875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"insufficient","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify probe non-happy-path behavior: project-not-found/auth-failure/timeout against Jira, empty-project (no issue types/statuses) responses, and missing/unwritable config file on --write.","cohort":["E3","E5","F4","G5","T6","T9","necessity","project.engine-layer-enforcement","project.portability"],"criteria":["T6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.4894,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'It calls the proven endpoints ... and emits a suggested mapping block' — only success flow described","No mention of project-not-found, auth failure, timeout, or empty-project responses in Approach or Testing","'--write merges it into the resolved config file' — no handling for a missing/unwritable config file"],"finding":"The probe command is a new user-facing CLI surface, but the plan handles only happy-path interrogation. Non-happy states are unaddressed: the target Jira project not existing (404), auth/permission failure, network timeout, and an empty/degenerate project (no issue types or statuses). For --write, the resolved config file not existing (or being unwritable) is also unhandled.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f54c4624c8a36ca5d","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach / Testing sections","norm_id":"nfa2dce50f9175ab0","priority":0.4606,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A user runs `rebar bridge probe BADKEY` against a nonexistent/unauthorized project and sees an unhandled exception or empty block instead of an actionable message","A project with zero configured issue types emits an empty/misleading mapping block silently"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Add Approach text and a test naming the error/empty paths (e.g. 404 -> actionable error, empty statuses -> explicit empty-vocabulary note, missing config file on --write -> create or error).","tier":"LLM","validity":0.6875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"insufficient","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the write-safety mechanism for --write (write-to-temp-then-atomic-rename, or read-modify-write with backup) so an interrupted write cannot corrupt the existing config.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e"],"criteria":["T5b"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.785,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'--write merges it into the resolved config file under projects.<KEY> (never clobbering existing hand edits — deep-merge, existing keys win)'","The 'failure-safe' test only asserts existing keys survive the MERGE logic, not that a crashed/failed write leaves the file intact."],"finding":"The --write path performs file I/O on the resolved config file but the plan does not specify write atomicity or partial-write safety (e.g. if the process is interrupted mid-write, is the original config preserved?).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f6c02e44e905a232b","impact":0.33,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach / '--write merges it into the resolved config file'","norm_id":"n2a8cd61e318fde1c","priority":0.165,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Probe crashes or disk error occurs while overwriting rebar.toml during --write, leaving a truncated/corrupt config."],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Add to Approach: '--write serializes the merged config to a temp file and atomically renames over the original, so a failed write leaves the prior config intact.' Add an AC/test for it.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State that --write writes the merged config atomically (temp-file + rename) so an interrupted write cannot corrupt or truncate existing hand edits.","cohort":["E3","E5","F4","G5","T6","T9","necessity","project.engine-layer-enforcement","project.portability"],"criteria":["T9"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.785,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'--write merges it into the resolved config file under projects.<KEY> (never clobbering existing hand edits — deep-merge, existing keys win)'","No statement of atomic write (temp-file + rename) or interrupted-write behavior for the config file"],"finding":"The --write path mutates a shared config file (rebar.toml) but the plan does not specify how the write is performed atomically or what happens under a concurrent/interrupted write. Deep-merge existing-keys-win gives idempotency across re-runs, but a crash mid-write or a concurrent editor is not addressed.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f978c27d46da7977b","impact":0.33,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach — '--write merges it into the resolved config file ... deep-merge, existing keys win'","norm_id":"n89db51076eaa4c57","priority":0.165,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A --write interrupted mid-flush leaves rebar.toml truncated/corrupt, losing the user's hand edits the merge was meant to preserve"],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Note atomic replacement of the config file and add a brief test that the pre-merge file is preserved on write-failure.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Capture the probe design decision (esp. why transitions are best-effort due to current-status-only API) in an ADR / AGENTS.md / design-doc note.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e"],"criteria":["T5e"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'Transitions are only partially discoverable (the API returns transitions from the current status only, not the full workflow graph)'","Scope lists a new module + CLI wiring + neutral emit/merge helper but no documentation artifact for the architectural rationale."],"finding":"The probe introduces a new command surface and a new probe/emit-merge pattern with a design decision (transitions are only partially discoverable from the current-status API) that is not captured in any ADR / AGENTS.md / design-doc update.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fc4dc116904c3440d","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope / Context","norm_id":"na542d81e7c415b5b","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A future maintainer wonders why transitions are flagged best-effort rather than fully populated and re-litigates the decision."],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add a failure/empty-response test with the faked REST client (empty issue-type list and/or an error status) asserting the probe's observable behavior.","cohort":["E3","E5","F4","G5","T6","T9","necessity","project.engine-layer-enforcement","project.portability"],"criteria":["E5"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'given canned /statuses, /issuetype, /issueLinkType, /priority responses, the emitted TOML contains the discovered vocabulary lists' — all fixtures are well-formed success cases","No failure/empty-response test named among the four listed tests or the four ACs"],"finding":"Testing enumerates only success-shaped fixtures (canned /statuses, /issuetype, etc.). No test exercises a failure or empty response from the faked REST client — e.g. an error status, an empty issue-type list, or a createmeta with no required-beyond-baseline fields.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fd4b9f021335d0496","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Testing section","norm_id":"ne17b4dce6702e44e","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An empty createmeta or empty statuses response produces a malformed or empty mapping block that no test guards against"],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State whether the --write helper reuses/extends the existing ADR-0070 writer (rebar._config_writer.write_jira_config / _emit_toml) — noting _emit_toml today rejects the nested projects.<KEY>.status_map tables the mapping block needs, so the plan must say it EXTENDS that emitter rather than building a parallel one.","cohort":["A1"],"criteria":["A1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["src/rebar/_config_writer.py:92 write_jira_config — 'read-whole / mutate / re-emit / atomic-replace writer'","src/rebar/_config_writer.py:32 _emit_toml — self-contained TOML emitter for rebar-owned files","docs/adr/0070-jira-onboard-config-write.md records the write-path decisions (stdlib-only, atomic, fail-closed)","CAVEAT: _emit_toml raises ConfigError beyond 'one level of [section]' (src/rebar/_config_writer.py:84-87) while the mapping block nests projects.KEY.status_map, so it cannot be reused unmodified — it must be extended"],"finding":"The plan's proposed 'neutral emit/merge helper' for the --write path risks rebuilding the existing ADR-0070 config writer (rebar._config_writer.write_jira_config / _emit_toml), which already implements read-whole-via-tomllib -> mutate dict -> atomic re-emit, stdlib-only and fail-closed.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f92758aba1109b1dd","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach / Scope ('a neutral emit/merge helper'; '--write merges 